# Copied or generated by Dead Letter > Audio > Import Audio (Editor/Audio/AudioImporter.cs). Git keeps one copy of each
# sound: art/sfx/out/ (the renders), game/undelivered/assets/music/ (the score) and, once it exists,
# game/undelivered/assets/voice/. The importer rebuilds these on each machine.
# Their .meta files are ignored too: the importer writes them with stable GUIDs (MD5 of the asset path), so they come
# out identical on every machine and SfxBank.asset's references survive. Committing them would only churn, as Unity
# deletes a .meta whose file is missing on a fresh clone.
/Sfx/*.wav
/Music/*.mp3
/Music/*.wav
/Voice/*.wav
/Voice/*.mp3
/Voice/*.ogg
/Sfx/*.wav.meta
/Music/*.mp3.meta
/Music/*.wav.meta
/Voice/*.wav.meta
/Voice/*.mp3.meta
/Voice/*.ogg.meta
# The importer's temporary copies of the padded loops (deleted after trimming).
/Music/Source/
/Music/Source.meta
